{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"agent_message","text":"The controls are now reproduced across pristine cycles: the upper control advances a six-phase movable bridge, while the lower control alternates a two-state rotation of the central assembly; neither is a generic “use” action. This mechanism does not match any existing leg, so I’m treating it as a new candidate rather than forcing an earlier bridge chain. I’ll now run a bounded clone BFS over exactly six actions (four moves plus those two clicks), keyed by the observable frame with only the turn-counter row removed. As a dense progress signal I’ll track the avatar’s minimum reached row and distinct reachable positions."}}
