{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_42","type":"agent_message","text":"The revealed selector has a verified four-state cycle: `(6,7) → (13,8) → (12,11) → (9,10) → …`; state 2 matches the top island’s `(12,11)` pad. Directly stepping on either upper glyph half still does nothing in all four states. I’ll now use the scaffold’s replay-based BFS from the verified upper checkpoint, initially excluding the lower bridge control, to test whether movement plus the rotator and selector can reach reward or even the top island. This keeps the state space bounded and directly falsifies the local-final-stage hypothesis if it exhausts."}}
