{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_411","type":"agent_message","text":"A second persistent trigger was hiding in plain sight: the upper glyph has two consumable 2×2 halves. The known route consumes only the right half; stepping on the left half permanently clears a different colored pattern. This is exactly the kind of dense progress transition we were missing. I’m now replaying both halves, then testing all four selector destinations from the hub."}}
